{"book":19,"chapter":23,"rubric":"PYTHON AS THE CONTROL PLANE / CHAPTER 23","slides":[{"title":"Steps or state","sub":"Chapter 23 · Python as the control plane","short":"State","main":"Describe the result instead of a list of steps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Steps","Repeat","State","Result"],"captions":["A script describes steps: do this, then that","A second run repeats everything: lines duplicate, commands fail","A description sets the result: a line, a package, a service in the right form","Idempotent: a repeated run changes nothing (changed=0)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"script: steps in order","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"script: steps in order","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a second run repeats it all","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"script: steps in order","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a second run repeats it all","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"description: what must exist","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"script: steps in order","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a second run repeats it all","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"description: what must exist","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"second run: changed=0","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.7,18.7,32.1]}]},{"title":"Where idempotence breaks","sub":"Chapter 23 · Python as the control plane","short":"Breakage","main":"Appending, useradd and mkdir break on the second run.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Append","Failure","Check","Harmless"],"captions":["echo >> appends a line on every run, the config grows","useradd on an existing name gives code 9, mkdir without -p fails","Check before changing: grep -qx for a line, id for a user","mkdir -p is idempotent itself; for the rest we write the check in code"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ useradd deploy","$ mkdir /srv/app","$ grep -qx 'Port 22' $F || echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ id deploy || useradd deploy","$ mkdir -p /srv/app"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ useradd deploy","$ mkdir /srv/app","$ grep -qx 'Port 22' $F || echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ id deploy || useradd deploy","$ mkdir -p /srv/app"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ useradd deploy","$ mkdir /srv/app","$ grep -qx 'Port 22' $F || echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ id deploy || useradd deploy","$ mkdir -p /srv/app"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ useradd deploy","$ mkdir /srv/app","$ grep -qx 'Port 22' $F || echo 'Port 22' >> $F","$ id deploy || useradd deploy","$ mkdir -p /srv/app"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[7.7,16.9,25.2]}]},{"title":"The ensure_line function","sub":"Chapter 23 · Python as the control plane","short":"ensure_line","main":"Read, compute, write on a difference, return changed.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Search","Last one","Equal","Edit"],"captions":["Search the pattern with re.search on each line, as lineinfile does","Take the last match; no match means the end of the list","The line is already right: change nothing, changed=False","Otherwise replace or add and return changed=True"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["def ensure_line(lines, line, regexp):","    hits = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines)","            if re.search(regexp, l)]","    i = hits[-1] if hits else len(lines)","    if i < len(lines) and lines[i] == line:","        return False","    lines[i:i + 1] = [line]","    return True"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["def ensure_line(lines, line, regexp):","    hits = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines)","            if re.search(regexp, l)]","    i = hits[-1] if hits else len(lines)","    if i < len(lines) and lines[i] == line:","        return False","    lines[i:i + 1] = [line]","    return True"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["def ensure_line(lines, line, regexp):","    hits = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines)","            if re.search(regexp, l)]","    i = hits[-1] if hits else len(lines)","    if i < len(lines) and lines[i] == line:","        return False","    lines[i:i + 1] = [line]","    return True"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["def ensure_line(lines, line, regexp):","    hits = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines)","            if re.search(regexp, l)]","    i = hits[-1] if hits else len(lines)","    if i < len(lines) and lines[i] == line:","        return False","    lines[i:i + 1] = [line]","    return True"],"hl":[6,7],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[11.4,21.0,30.7]}]},{"title":"Dry-run and diff","sub":"Chapter 23 · Python as the control plane","short":"Dry-run","main":"The same code without the write, and a diff of what would change.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Tools","Ansible","Diff","Limit"],"captions":["apt-get -s and rsync -n show actions withou